// FLESH / FIRMWARE
// Neon rain falls through an illegal rooftop concert. Robots wield the
// instruments; humans plug into the mixing desk and livecode their nerves.
// Every keystroke changes a throat, a pulse, a memory. The city listens.
// Industrial electro / cyberpunk opera without words. D minor, 128 BPM.
// All voices use bundled drums or synthesis; no external samples required.
//
// FORM: 128 bars / 4:00, then loops. One cycle = one 4/4 bar.
//   boot       8  e1  0:00  Rain on the server district; a machine wakes.
//   robots    16  e3  0:15  Chrome musicians assemble a precise broken beat.
//   humans    16  e3  0:45  Livecoders become formant instruments, answering.
//   chorus    16  e4  1:15  Flesh and firmware share the eight-note hook.
//   blackout   8  e1  1:45  Corporate ICE cuts the grid; hearts keep time.
//   jailbreak 16  e4  2:00  A human solo rewrites the robot orchestra.
//   uprising  32  e5  2:30  Full ensemble; the hook returns an octave higher.
//   dawn      16  e1  3:30  The city exhales; the terminal cursor survives.
//
// ROBOT motif: D A C A / F E D rest — hard FM, left of center.
// HUMAN answer: rest D F A / C A G E — breathy vowels, right of center.
// CHORUS hook: D F A C / A G E D. Blackout suspends it; dawn resolves it.
// Imagined refrain (instrumental score, no synthesized spoken lyrics):
//   "Chrome hands play us / we type the rain.
//    Flesh is the waveform / nobody owns the mainframe."

setbpm(128);

"<boot@2 robots@4 humans@4 chorus@4 blackout@2 jailbreak@4 uprising@8 dawn@4>".slow(4).pickRestart({
  boot: stack(
    note("<[d3,a3,e4] [d3,a3,f4]>").slow(4).s("wt_pad")
      .attack(1.2).release(2.0).lpf(950).chorus(0.3).room(0.65).gain(0.13).pan(0.4),
    s("hh*16").hpf(7200).gain("[0.015 0.025 0.01 0.04]*4")
